WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.194
Episode twelve: the agents from the command line.

2
00:00:03.194 --> 00:00:06.974
This video assumes APEX installed as the README describes.

3
00:00:06.974 --> 00:00:09.582
Run every command below from its folder.

4
00:00:09.582 --> 00:00:16.388
That is episode one, plus Claude Code, installed and logged in.

5
00:00:16.388 --> 00:00:18.653
The agents need one thing first.

6
00:00:18.653 --> 00:00:20.493
A finished run to look at.

7
00:00:20.493 --> 00:00:23.112
The README's first example makes one.

8
00:00:23.112 --> 00:00:40.551
Its run folder is examples/linear_gaussian/runs/linear_esmda.

9
00:00:40.551 --> 00:00:47.432
The agents use [agents.llm] in service.toml, in the services root; here the default one, in the home folder.

10
00:00:47.432 --> 00:00:50.044
The model is Claude, through Claude Code.

11
00:00:50.044 --> 00:01:00.130
The calls count against your subscription's usage.

12
00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:08.162
The agents use APEX's tools, and tool clients read only the service's workspace folders unless service.toml adds more.

13
00:01:08.162 --> 00:01:12.178
So we add the absolute path of your APEX folder's examples.

14
00:01:12.178 --> 00:01:21.337
Type your own folder's absolute path here.

15
00:01:21.337 --> 00:01:25.351
We check the model with a first answer through the model.

16
00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:42.854
Good to know: Every agent except apex agent ask also works without a model, with --no-llm: it then decides by its rules only.

17
00:01:42.854 --> 00:01:47.970
We ask which localization methods APEX has, and which is the default.

18
00:01:47.970 --> 00:02:08.677
The agent answers with APEX's tools: plugins, schemas, validation, runs and jobs.

19
00:02:08.677 --> 00:02:10.181
Now the run itself.

20
00:02:10.181 --> 00:02:13.189
We keep its folder in a variable, RUN.

21
00:02:13.189 --> 00:02:23.874
RUN may also be a run id or a job id.

22
00:02:23.874 --> 00:02:27.002
The monitor asks: is it healthy, should it stop?

23
00:02:27.002 --> 00:02:46.132
In each agent, code computes the facts and named rules decide first.

24
00:02:46.132 --> 00:02:50.182
Diagnosis gives causes, and what to change (with validated patches).

25
00:02:50.182 --> 00:03:13.696
The model then judges with read-only tools, and its answer is held to the facts: a finding no rule backs is dropped, and each correction is printed.

26
00:03:13.696 --> 00:03:17.721
The report agent writes a narrative of the results, in Markdown.

27
00:03:17.721 --> 00:03:36.697
Every call is recorded in the run's agents/ folder, prompt included.

28
00:03:36.697 --> 00:03:53.156
The plotter draws figures from a request in words: here, box plots of the data mismatch.

29
00:03:53.156 --> 00:04:04.383
This is one of the figures it drew.

30
00:04:04.383 --> 00:04:09.759
The planner writes a study within the budget, revising it when validation refuses it.

31
00:04:09.759 --> 00:04:17.727
Here the question is whether a longer inflation schedule improves the RMSE, within a budget of twenty thousand simulator runs.

32
00:04:17.727 --> 00:04:37.384
It submits nothing unless you add --submit and confirm.

33
00:04:37.384 --> 00:04:46.302
The other way round: Claude Code can call APEX's tools in a conversation: list plugins, validate and submit runs, read results.

34
00:04:46.302 --> 00:04:48.830
This command registers APEX with it.

35
00:04:48.830 --> 00:05:03.857
--budget-runs limits the simulator runs this session may submit.

36
00:05:03.857 --> 00:05:09.357
Thank you for watching.
